 "title": "Comparative Analysis of Mitochondrial Retrograde Signaling in Yeast and Human Cells",
 "summary": "This cluster focuses on the comparative analysis of mitochondrial retrograde signaling in Saccharomyces cerevisiae and human cells. Oksana Tehlivets is involved in the conceptualization of S-adenosyl-L-homocysteine, which is associated with indole, and indole is associated with indoxyl. The CON-DLY group has a significant difference in comparison to the SC-DLY group, and the CON-DLY group has a higher concentration of skatole. Skatole is associated with indole, and indole is associated with indoxyl. The SC-DLY group has a higher abundance of Proteobacteria. The study uses Genomics and Proteomics methods to analyze the data. The results show that Saccharomyces cerevisiae has conserved pathways with human cells and has mitochondrial retrograde signaling and nitrogen metabolism.",
